From e2283178c0db04d5a857d96920e31f54466a7a72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hector Isaza <76170012+hecisaza@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:27:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] server: a tool-call block too short to hold the DSML block it
 opens with is read as no DSML block, not a slice past the payload's start

tool_parse.parseEnvelopes read any envelope payload that opens with a DSML opener as a whole DSML block, cutting the opener from its start and a closer's length from its end. A <tool_call> (or <|tool_call>, <x:tool_call>) payload can open with a DSML opener and be shorter than opener and closer together; the slice's end then falls before its start. dsmlBlock returns that slice only when the payload is long enough. A shorter one goes the way of any tool-call block that is not a call: no call; a whole reply with no call limit keeps it as text, a one-call reply drops it. Every payload long enough reads exactly as before.

Tests: tool_parse_test.zig (the parse, both spellings, the boundaries, the call limits, both live streamers) and dsml_stream_test.zig (end to end: the chat route whole and streamed at four round sizes, with and without the one-call policy and reasoning first, then the next request on the same server; and over HTTP through the chat, Responses and Messages routes).
